      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rhome began as Prairie Point, a crossroads settlement founded by Missourians in the late 1850s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofrhome.com/community/history.php",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1862 Prairie Point boasted a hotel, a school, and several businesses, making it Wise County’s second‑largest town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofrhome.com/community/history.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Civil War, a small brigade of older men and boys defended the area, yet it remained vulnerable to Indian and bandit attacks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofrhome.com/community/history.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The railroad arrived in 1882, and the new settlement was renamed Rhome in 1883 to honor Colonel Rhome.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
